WEBVTT

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:23.708
I was in the library
the other night

00:00:23.751 --> 00:00:26.711
in the Restricted Section,

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:30.584
and I read something rather odd
about a bit of rare magic.

00:00:31.672 --> 00:00:35.720
It's called,
as I understand it,

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:37.200
a Horcrux.

00:00:38.897 --> 00:00:42.031
I beg your pardon?Horcrux.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:44.903
I came across the term
while reading

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:48.080
and I didn't
fully understand it.

00:00:48.124 --> 00:00:49.777
I'm not sure
what you were reading, Tom,

00:00:49.821 --> 00:00:52.737
but this is very dark stuff,
very dark indeed.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.305
Which is...

00:00:55.348 --> 00:00:58.047
why I came to you.

00:01:00.049 --> 00:01:02.616
A Horcrux is an object
in which a person

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.880
has concealed
part of their soul.

00:01:05.924 --> 00:01:08.666
But I don't understand
how that works, sir.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:15.151
One splits one's soul and hides
part of it in an object.

00:01:15.194 --> 00:01:16.674
By doing so,
you're protected,

00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:19.024
should you be attacked
and your body destroyed.

00:01:19.068 --> 00:01:20.417
Protected?

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.987
That part of your soul
that is hidden lives on.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.033
In other words, you cannot die.

00:01:34.605 --> 00:01:37.825
And how does one
split his soul, sir?

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:41.351
I think you already know
the answer to that, Tom.

00:01:41.394 --> 00:01:43.918
Murder.

00:01:43.962 --> 00:01:45.833
Yes.

00:01:45.877 --> 00:01:48.184
Killing rips
the soul apart.

00:01:48.227 --> 00:01:50.969
It is a violation
against nature.

00:01:51.013 --> 00:01:54.320
RIDDLE:
Can you only
split the soul once?

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:56.540
For instance, isn't seven--?

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.759
Seven?

00:01:58.803 --> 00:02:00.674
Merlin's beard, Tom.

00:02:00.718 --> 00:02:04.156
Isn't it bad enough
to consider killing one person?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.118
To rip the soul
into seven pieces...

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:12.382
This is all hypothetical,
isn't it, Tom? All academic?

00:02:16.908 --> 00:02:18.518
Of course, sir.

00:02:20.999 --> 00:02:23.436
It'll be our little secret.

00:02:32.054 --> 00:02:33.838
HARRY:
Sir.

00:02:48.722 --> 00:02:51.029
This is beyond anything
I imagined.

00:02:51.073 --> 00:02:53.901
You mean to say he succeeded,
sir, in making a Horcrux?

00:02:53.945 --> 00:02:57.122
Oh, yes, he succeeded,
all right. And not just once.

00:02:57.166 --> 00:02:58.602
What are they exactly?

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:02.649
Could be anything.
Most commonplace of objects.

00:03:04.956 --> 00:03:06.697
DUMBLEDORE:
A ring, for example.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.917
Or a book.

00:03:09.961 --> 00:03:12.529
Tom Riddle's diary.It's a Horcrux, yes.

00:03:12.572 --> 00:03:15.053
Four years ago, when you saved
Ginny Weasley's life

00:03:15.097 --> 00:03:17.055
in the Chamber of Secrets,
you brought me this.

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:19.753
I knew then this was
a different kind of magic.

00:03:19.797 --> 00:03:22.365
Very dark, very powerful.

00:03:22.408 --> 00:03:24.932
But until tonight
I had no idea just how powerful.

00:03:24.976 --> 00:03:27.065
And the ring?Belonged to Voldemort's mother.

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:29.023
Difficult to find.

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:32.157
Even more difficult to destroy.

00:03:32.201 --> 00:03:34.420
But if you could find them all,

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.248
if you did destroy
each Horcrux--

00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:39.208
One destroys Voldemort.But how would you find them?

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.644
They could be hidden anywhere.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:44.387
True. But magic,
especially dark magic--

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.997
[SCREAM]

00:03:57.835 --> 00:04:00.272
Leaves traces.

00:04:07.584 --> 00:04:09.716
It's where you've been going,
isn't it, sir?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.241
When you leave the school?Yes.

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:16.114
And I think perhaps
I may have found another.

00:04:16.158 --> 00:04:20.597
But this time, I cannot hope
to destroy it alone.

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:23.948
Once again,

00:04:23.991 --> 00:04:27.169
I must ask
too much of you, Harry.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.913
Have you ever considered
that you ask too much,

00:04:32.957 --> 00:04:35.699
that you take
too much for granted?

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:38.310
Has it ever crossed
your brilliant mind

00:04:38.354 --> 00:04:40.921
that I don't want
to do this anymore?

00:04:40.965 --> 00:04:43.228
Whether it has or hasn't
is irrelevant.

00:04:43.272 --> 00:04:46.100
DUMBLEDORE:
I will not negotiate with you,
Severus.

00:04:46.144 --> 00:04:50.235
You agreed.
Nothing more to discuss.

00:05:08.122 --> 00:05:09.994
Oh, Harry.

00:05:12.301 --> 00:05:15.304
You need a shave,
my friend.

00:05:17.393 --> 00:05:21.832
You know, at times,
I forget how much you've grown.

00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:26.184
At times, I still see
the small boy from the cupboard.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:30.188
Forgive my mawkishness, Harry.

00:05:30.232 --> 00:05:31.842
I'm an old man.

00:05:31.885 --> 00:05:33.713
You still look the same to me,
sir.

00:05:35.019 --> 00:05:37.630
Just like your mother,
you're unfailingly kind.

00:05:37.674 --> 00:05:41.808
A trait people never fail
to undervalue, I'm afraid.

00:05:44.158 --> 00:05:48.772
The place to which we journey
tonight is extremely dangerous.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:52.428
I promised you could accompany
me, and I stand by that promise.

00:05:52.471 --> 00:05:54.430
But there is one condition:

00:05:54.473 --> 00:05:57.824
You must obey every command
I give you, without question.

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:00.262
Yes, sir.

00:06:00.305 --> 00:06:03.003
You do understand
what I'm saying?

00:06:03.047 --> 00:06:05.702
Should I tell you to hide,
you hide.

00:06:05.745 --> 00:06:08.270
Should I tell you to run,
you run.

00:06:08.313 --> 00:06:11.229
Should I tell you to abandon me
and save yourself,

00:06:11.273 --> 00:06:13.100
you must do so.

00:06:13.144 --> 00:06:15.146
[♪♪♪]

00:06:17.366 --> 00:06:19.150
Your word, Harry.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.893
My word.

00:06:22.936 --> 00:06:25.939
Take my arm.

00:06:25.983 --> 00:06:28.594
Sir, I thought you couldn't
Apparate within Hogwarts.

00:06:28.638 --> 00:06:32.685
Well,
being me has its privileges.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:43.435
[♪♪♪]

